# =============================================================================
# BUILD 02 (FAILED ATTEMPT): First-Instinct Collatz, Modulo & Newton Solver
# =============================================================================

Stones is a collection.
Each stone has an id (number), a val (number) and steps (number).
No two stones share the same id.
Reject duplicates.

# FAILURE 1: '%' is in the lexicon, but mapped to PCT ("percent"), NOT modulo!
even-stones: show the stones whose val % 2 is 0.

# FAILURE 2: "modulo" / "remainder" are not in the lexicon
odd-stones: show the stones whose val modulo 2 is 1.

# FAILURE 3: Newton-Raphson square root step divides by a variable field (val)
newton-sqrt: for every stone, set val to (val + 10000 / val) / 2.

# FAILURE 4: No while/until loop construct to iterate a single command until convergence
solve-collatz: while val is over 1, halve val.
